From bebee3881f7dd6fff83c6912b254994d2703a866 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:36:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] [drop] release a foreign box of trivially copyable
 members in place

`prepareWorklistDropBridges` wraps every foreign drop function: the body
moves to `<name>.worklist.<order>`, and for the last reference the
function joins or starts a destruction scope around it. The scope is
there for the work the body may enqueue. A shared box whose payload is
trivially copyable enqueues none: its release only frees the box, which
is how `WorklistGlue::release` already treats it (`isTriviallyCopyable`,
then `emitBoxFree`). Closure drops with trivially copyable payloads are
exempt for the same reason.

Such a foreign drop now keeps its body, a decrement and the free at the
last reference. A payload with a managed member (another box, a foreign
object, a big integer, a token) and a regional box keep the bridge. The
behaviour is the same: inside a drain the bridge called the body
directly, and outside one it opened a scope around a body that queues
nothing, drained an empty list and found no scope-exit callback, since
those are queued only inside a scope.

The cost was one runtime entry (`__reussir_drop_join_or_run`, a
thread-local test, a scope and an indirect call) per final release from
Rust code. Measured with a prototype of this change on a program that
keeps a 64-byte record of floats in a Rust array and drops the old
element at every store: 34.2 ms to 22.8 ms (median of 9; ratio 0.667,
minimum 0.665), 19 other programs in the same step between 0.984 and
1.005, all outputs equal. This form has not been timed; for that
program it gives the release function and its caller the same eight
instructions as the prototype (the decrement and
`__reussir_deallocate(p, 8, 64)`).

Tests: conversion/worklist_drop_bridges_leaf.mlir (a record of scalars,
a record of value records, a variant of them and an atomic box keep
their bodies under both drop orders; a record with a link to another
box, one with a foreign object and a rigid box get the bridge),
frontend/ffi_leaf_release_e2e.rr (a Rust `Vec` of such records and of an
enum with nullary arms: no call to `__reussir_drop_join_or_run` in their
release functions, one in the release of a record that holds a box; the
program runs under both drop orders).
